src/content/docs/guides/Tips-n-Tricks/define-environment-variables.mdoc:for workspace-specific settings (like the [Nx Cloud token](/ci/recipes/security/access-tokens)).
src/content/docs/extending-nx/create-install-package.mdoc:Customizing your initial project setup is already possible with an [Nx Preset generator](/docs/extending-nx/guides/create-preset). By creating and shipping a generator named `preset` in your Nx plugin, you can then pass it via the `--preset` flag to the `create-nx-workspace` command:
src/content/docs/extending-nx/create-install-package.mdoc:This will invoke the `my-plugin` package's `preset` generator, which will contain the logic for setting up the workspace. This preset generator will be invoked when running either `npx create-nx-workspace --preset my-plugin` or `npx create-my-plugin`. For more information about customizing your preset, see: [Creating a Preset](/docs/extending-nx/guides/create-preset).
src/content/docs/guides/Adopting Nx/from-turborepo.mdoc:| `envMode`              | Nx core does not block any environment variables. See [React](/docs/technologies/react/recipes/use-environment-variables-in-react) and [Angular](/docs/technologies/angular/recipes/use-environment-variables-in-angular) guides |
